    <span class="accordion__number">3</span>
    Learning objectives
    <span class="accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
  </button>
  <div class="accordion__content">
    <div class="accordion__body">
<p>By the end of this unit, you should be able to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Explain what Nietzsche means by a "genealogy" of morality and why he thinks this kind of inquiry matters.</li>
<li>Describe the distinction between master morality (good/bad) and slave morality (good/evil), and explain how each originates according to Nietzsche.</li>
<li>Explain the concept of <em>ressentiment</em> and the role it plays in the emergence of slave morality.</li>
<li>Describe Nietzsche's account of the "slave revolt in morality" and the historical forces he associates with it.</li>
<li>Explain Nietzsche's critique of the "English psychologists" and what he thinks they get wrong about the origin of moral concepts.</li>
<li>Articulate and assess the challenge that genealogical debunking poses to the authority of moral concepts.</li>
</ul>
